From 9abe659051090b1d58eba84603172d20d6ff3b2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Preston Hervey <preston.hervey@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 21:56:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add Microsoft Fabric Lakehouse (Spark) platform

Adds a new platform, fabric_spark, that runs bruin assets against
Microsoft Fabric Lakehouses using Spark SQL as the compute engine with
first-class PySpark support, driven through the Fabric Lakehouse Livy
API (the same interface as Microsoft's dbt-fabricspark adapter). The
existing fabric platform targets Fabric Warehouse over the SQL/TDS
endpoint; this fills the Lakehouse/Spark gap.

New package pkg/fabricspark:
- Livy REST client: session lifecycle, sql/pyspark statements, Azure AD
  service principal (client credentials, cached tokens) or static token
  auth, retries with backoff, 429 Retry-After handling, transient-404
  tolerance, transparent expired-session recovery
- DB client implementing the standard connection interfaces (Select,
  SelectWithSchema, RunQueryWithoutResult, Ping, CreateSchemaIfNotExist,
  GetDatabases/GetTables/GetColumns) plus RunPySpark
- Delta materializations: view, create+replace (partitioning / liquid
  clustering), append, merge, delete+insert, truncate+insert,
  time_interval, ddl, incremental SCD2 (scd2_by_column / scd2_by_time,
  requires Fabric runtime 1.3+ for WHEN NOT MATCHED BY SOURCE), and a
  new anti_join strategy: insert-only incremental via null-safe LEFT
  ANTI JOIN on the asset's primary_key columns, self-bootstrapping and
  optionally bounded to the run window
- Asset types: fabric.spark.sql, fabric.spark.pyspark (runs in the same
  Spark session as SQL assets), fabric.spark.seed (native CSV loader),
  fabric.spark.sensor.query, fabric.spark.sensor.table (SHOW TABLES
  prober; lakehouses expose no information_schema)
- Optional high-concurrency mode: pools REPLs from Fabric's
  /highConcurrencySessions API so parallel assets execute concurrently
  inside one Spark application
- ingestr integration via the OneLake destination URI
- Column checks incl. Spark-specific accepted_values and RLIKE pattern

Registration: pipeline asset types + anti_join strategy, config
connection type fabric_spark, connection manager, executor defaults,
run/render wiring, lint (table sensor allowlist, platform name,
anti_join validation), jinja platform overrides (Spark dialect),
sqlglot dialect mapping, and a docs page.

Tests: 50 test functions (100 cases) including an in-process mock of
the Fabric Livy API covering session lifecycle, statement submit/poll,
high-concurrency REPL pooling/recovery, throttling and session expiry;
suite is race-clean and needs no Fabric capacity. Verified end-to-end
with the built CLI: bruin validate and bruin render against a
fabric.spark.sql pipeline.

